    <h2 class="p7-section-title">Dual-rail · 6-wheel alternator array · crankless enclosed oil drivetrain</h2>
    <p class="p7-section-lead">
        Phase 7 replaces the Phase 6 rotary converter wheel pair with two full independent steam rails,
        each driving three cycloidal wheels. Six total wheels spin six dedicated 150A alternators.
        Their combined AC output feeds a shared step-down transformer → bridge rectifier → PCW-managed
        resistor-regulated feedback loop. The enclosed oil crankless engine converts wheel-lobe motion
        to continuous rotational output through roller followers and an eccentric shaft — no piston seals,
        no combustion gases, no oil contamination from steam.
    </p>

